WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:03.503
-Our next guest is a very funny
comedian whose stand-up special

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:05.805
"Ms. Pat: Y'all want to hear
something crazy?"

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:07.073
is available on Netflix.

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:09.642
She also created and stars
in "The Ms. Pat Show."

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:13.212
The second season is streaming
now on BET+.

00:00:13.212 --> 00:00:14.748
Let's take a look.

00:00:22.589 --> 00:00:23.857
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.592 --> 00:00:28.862
-Tell her she pretty.

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:31.030
-What?

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:34.567
-Tell her she pretty.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:36.135
-[Bleep] you.

00:00:36.135 --> 00:00:37.470
[ Laughter ]

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.140
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:43.342 --> 00:00:45.277
That's why you're dead [bleep].

00:00:45.277 --> 00:00:48.314
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:51.884
-Please welcome back to the show
Ms. Pat, everybody.

00:00:51.884 --> 00:00:53.653
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:53.653 --> 00:01:01.461 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:09.235 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:11.637
Welcome back.

00:01:11.637 --> 00:01:13.806
-Thank you.
I'm in person this time.

00:01:13.806 --> 00:01:15.808
-You're in person.
We had you on Zoom last time,

00:01:15.808 --> 00:01:18.344
which was fantastic,
but it's the real deal today,

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:19.512
and we're very excited.
-It's the real deal.

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:21.147
-I got to see you in person
at the Emmys.

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:24.183
Your show was nominated for
Best Directing for a Sitcom.

00:01:24.183 --> 00:01:26.519
-Yes. I was so excited.

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:28.187
I could not believe
I was at the Emmys.

00:01:28.187 --> 00:01:30.423
I wasn't -- You know, I didn't
need the dust collector

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:32.992
'cause the, director was up
for nomination.

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:34.694
I call the little trophy
the dust collector.

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:36.996
-Oh, gotcha.
-I was there for the food,

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:38.697
and it was great.
-It was good food.

00:01:38.697 --> 00:01:43.169
You were also at -- Norman Lear,
the incredible television writer

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:45.705
and producer who's made,
you know, so many iconic shows

00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:49.475
over the years, he just had a
100th birthday party celebration

00:01:49.475 --> 00:01:50.843
that you were at.

00:01:50.843 --> 00:01:52.678
What was your experience
with Norman?

00:01:52.678 --> 00:01:55.448
-You know, the party was running
a little late for me.

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:57.617
So I'm usually in bed by 8:30
when I'm home.

00:01:57.617 --> 00:01:59.251
So when I got up to speak,
I was like,

00:01:59.251 --> 00:02:02.221
"Norman Lear, how you still
awake? You 100 and I'm 50."

00:02:02.221 --> 00:02:03.489
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.489 --> 00:02:05.991
"I know these people got
a battery pack in you.

00:02:05.991 --> 00:02:07.660
Are you still alive, Mr. Lear?"

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:09.329
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:11.631
-But it must've been so cool
that he's a fan of your show.

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:14.234
-It was cool, but it was also
cool to see

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:17.069
a 100-year-old person
up past 8:30.

00:02:17.069 --> 00:02:18.538
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:02:18.538 --> 00:02:21.240
That's his real accomplishment.
-That's his real accomplishment.

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:23.142
'Cause I'm 50, and 8:30,
I'm out.

00:02:23.142 --> 00:02:24.410
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:26.879
I take this wig and this bra off
and it's over.

00:02:26.879 --> 00:02:29.682
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:31.717
-It's good that it's not
time-released at 8:30,

00:02:31.717 --> 00:02:33.051
and then if you're out
in public, that'd be --

00:02:33.051 --> 00:02:34.520
-Oh, it is time-released.

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:36.356
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:40.159
-You pull from your life
in your wonderful sitcom.

00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:42.494
You have eight kids.
You have three grandkids.

00:02:42.494 --> 00:02:45.130
How do they feel about the fact
that your show

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:47.200
is a little bit
autobiographical?

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:50.435
-You know, they all excited,
but I have four kids

00:02:50.435 --> 00:02:51.837
that somebody gave to me.

00:02:51.837 --> 00:02:54.474
I'm not gonna say I adopted them
'cause somebody dropped them off

00:02:54.474 --> 00:02:56.309
and said,
"These are your crack babies."

00:02:56.309 --> 00:02:57.476
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.476 --> 00:02:59.979
And so I never adopted
anybody's kids.

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:02.649
They always give 'em to me.
-Okay.

00:03:02.649 --> 00:03:05.651
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.651 --> 00:03:07.487
-And they don't never come
insured, either.

00:03:07.487 --> 00:03:09.222
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.222 --> 00:03:12.324
So, the new babies
that I'm raising,

00:03:12.324 --> 00:03:13.492
they're a little bougie.

00:03:13.492 --> 00:03:14.961
They come up to me one day
and they said,

00:03:14.961 --> 00:03:16.930
"We Googled you and we're rich."

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:20.066
I said, "Get those dirty drawers
and let's wash our underwear."

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:21.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:22.534
"Ain't nobody rich
in this house.

00:03:22.534 --> 00:03:23.736
We all do the same thing."

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:25.004
-Yeah, you can't let 'em --

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:27.105
You can't let kids start
thinking there's money to spend.

00:03:27.105 --> 00:03:29.475
-Oh, you can't let anybody think
there's money to spend.

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:30.643
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:32.011
Do you have that problem with
your family?

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:34.046
-Yeah. I have a brother
who told me

00:03:34.046 --> 00:03:36.049
I should invest in his tow truck
company.

00:03:36.049 --> 00:03:38.251
But I was like, "You just got
out of federal penitentiary.

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:40.953
You got a leg monitor."

00:03:40.953 --> 00:03:43.823
You can't tow no trucks.
You can't go past the mailbox."

00:03:43.823 --> 00:03:48.394
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:51.296
"You need a better investment,
brother."

00:03:51.296 --> 00:03:54.299
-When they come to you with
their investment ideas,

00:03:54.299 --> 00:03:56.135
do you ever try to point them in
another direction?

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:57.570
-No. I'm honest.

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.104
I tell people, I said,
I didn't give you --

00:03:59.104 --> 00:04:00.740
You know I'm an ex-drug dealer.

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:02.375
"I didn't give you
my crack-dealing money.

00:04:02.375 --> 00:04:04.009
I used to forge white people
checks.

00:04:04.009 --> 00:04:05.611
I didn't give you
none of that money."

00:04:05.611 --> 00:04:09.048
Black people keep starting
their checking accounts over.

00:04:09.048 --> 00:04:11.550
"And I'm not gonna give you
any of my TV money."

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:13.085
[ Laughter ]
-So that's good.

00:04:13.085 --> 00:04:14.487
You just laid down the law
early.

00:04:14.487 --> 00:04:16.555
-I say no. "I'm not gonna give
you nothing.

00:04:16.555 --> 00:04:18.391
Go get a job."
-But this is very nice.

00:04:18.391 --> 00:04:21.227
Is it true that you encouraged
your husband to retire?

00:04:21.227 --> 00:04:24.129
-Yes. After the first season,
I lived in Indiana.

00:04:24.129 --> 00:04:26.098
I'm from Atlanta,
and I wanted to go home,

00:04:26.098 --> 00:04:27.934
and I told my husband,
"I'm never coming back.

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:29.535
You need to retire."
-Yeah.

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:31.304
-And so now, he's just doing
foolish stuff,

00:04:31.304 --> 00:04:32.672
and I still wish he had his job.

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:33.873
[ Laughter ]

00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:35.908
-Oh, it backfired a little bit?
Did it backfire?

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:37.276
-He just buying toys.

00:04:37.276 --> 00:04:40.780
He bought a $4,000 drone that --
we both 50 -- don't know

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:43.449
how to fly it,
and it gets stuck in the air.

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:45.017
And I'm like,
"Just hit it with a rock."

00:04:45.017 --> 00:04:48.421
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.421 --> 00:04:50.823
-So he's not really good with
sort of gadgets.

00:04:50.823 --> 00:04:53.725
-No, not technology.
Now, he can build you a house

00:04:53.725 --> 00:04:55.161
or he can build you a doghouse.

00:04:55.161 --> 00:04:57.396
But he don't know nothing about
electronics.

00:04:57.396 --> 00:05:00.399
And he always blame it on
"I can't see. I need glasses."

00:05:00.399 --> 00:05:02.835
No, you don't.
You're too old for technology.

00:05:02.835 --> 00:05:04.703
[ Laughter ]

00:05:04.703 --> 00:05:07.473
-This is very exciting
'cause season two is airing.

00:05:07.473 --> 00:05:09.908
Season three is done.
-Season three is done.

00:05:09.908 --> 00:05:11.177
-You've got
a stand-up special out

00:05:11.177 --> 00:05:12.578
and you're going on the road.
Do you feel like,

00:05:12.578 --> 00:05:15.848
with all this success,
is your fan base is changing?

00:05:15.848 --> 00:05:17.983
-My fan base actually got black.

00:05:17.983 --> 00:05:20.352
-What?
-I'm real-real black.

00:05:20.352 --> 00:05:22.421
You can see that, right?
Well, not real-real black,

00:05:22.421 --> 00:05:24.323
Wesley Snipes black,
but I'm black.

00:05:24.323 --> 00:05:27.994
[ Laughter ]

00:05:27.994 --> 00:05:31.230
I'm culturally black, okay?

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:34.600
For years, I did Joe Rogan,
Bert Kreischer, all of that,

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:36.935
you know, white stuff,
let's be honest.

00:05:36.935 --> 00:05:39.605
And when I did BET+,
the black people are like,

00:05:39.605 --> 00:05:41.106
"Oh, my God. You're my aunty."

00:05:41.106 --> 00:05:42.809
I'm like, "Where was y'all at
when I needed y'all?"

00:05:42.809 --> 00:05:44.310
[ Laughter ]

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:47.246
But I love the diversity that I
bring that I can talk about,

00:05:47.246 --> 00:05:49.949
"Hi, I grew up and where I'm
from in Atlanta."

00:05:49.949 --> 00:05:52.618
And no matter what your race is,
everybody can relate.

00:05:52.618 --> 00:05:55.120
-I think everybody can relate,
especially to the struggle,

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:56.655
and I think people are really
excited excited when they

00:05:56.655 --> 00:05:59.424
see you because they understand
how you worked so hard.

00:05:59.424 --> 00:06:01.327
And obviously, you've got this
natural talent,

00:06:01.327 --> 00:06:03.229
but I don't think any any of it
would've happened without...

00:06:03.229 --> 00:06:04.830
-Being shot
-...this incredible work ethic.

00:06:04.830 --> 00:06:06.732
-Being in jail,
having kids young.

00:06:06.732 --> 00:06:08.634
I needed a little struggle.

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:10.769
-But I want to say,
you've got grandkids now.

00:06:10.769 --> 00:06:12.105
You must thrive
as a grandmother.

00:06:12.105 --> 00:06:13.706
Do they love you?
-I do.

00:06:13.706 --> 00:06:15.974
I have twin grandsons,
one cute, one ugly.

00:06:15.974 --> 00:06:19.444
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:19.444 --> 00:06:21.046
-I just said that
on national TV.

00:06:21.046 --> 00:06:23.583
-Well, you didn't say which one
was which, so they don't know.

00:06:23.583 --> 00:06:25.851
[ Laughter ]

00:06:25.851 --> 00:06:29.254
Don't name names.
-You know what's crazy?

00:06:29.254 --> 00:06:31.858
One of them is really ugly.
But he --

00:06:31.858 --> 00:06:33.292
[ Laughter ]

00:06:33.292 --> 00:06:35.594
And she gave -- What's so crazy?

00:06:35.594 --> 00:06:37.663
I hate people that give me
newborn pictures.

00:06:37.663 --> 00:06:39.665
So she gives me pictures of them
when they a baby, and I'm like,

00:06:39.665 --> 00:06:41.100
"I'm not putting this mess
on my wall."

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:43.235
[ Laughter ]
"Come back in eight months

00:06:43.235 --> 00:06:45.504
when they stop looking like
whatever this is."

00:06:45.504 --> 00:06:47.806
[ Laughter ]

00:06:47.806 --> 00:06:49.242
-It's very nice to have someone

00:06:49.242 --> 00:06:51.376
both loving and honest
in your life.

00:06:51.376 --> 00:06:53.546
-One of my grandsons
look like he smoke weed.

00:06:53.546 --> 00:06:57.883
[ Laughter ]

00:06:57.883 --> 00:06:59.552
-How old is he?
-Five.

00:06:59.552 --> 00:07:02.654
[ Laughter ]

00:07:02.654 --> 00:07:04.557
But he look like
my side of the family.

00:07:04.557 --> 00:07:06.726
I'm like,
"Baby, you never did alcohol,

00:07:06.726 --> 00:07:08.527
but you took on
an alcoholic face."

00:07:08.527 --> 00:07:10.162
[ Laughter ]

00:07:10.162 --> 00:07:12.999
-Well, that's a lovely thing
to pass down to your kids.

00:07:12.999 --> 00:07:15.100
Hey, I'm so happy you're here.
-Thank you.

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:16.936
-It is just such a pleasure
to see you in person.

00:07:16.936 --> 00:07:18.704
And congratulations on
all your success.

00:07:18.704 --> 00:07:19.872
You guys --
-Thank you.

00:07:19.872 --> 00:07:21.440
-Ms. Pat.

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:24.176
Season two of "The Ms. Pat Show"
is streaming now on BET+.

00:07:24.176 --> 00:07:25.211
We'll be right back.

